1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--unassisted-writing","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/unassisted-writing","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/unassisted-writing","sourceHash":"dfe8a1c141776f0ea14b303d14212402b444d756eb45ae915583207a32131910","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:21.188Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Unassisted Writing","zh":"无辅助写作"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Unassisted writing means writing in the target language without any tools — no dictionary, no grammar checker, no AI help. Just you and your brain.","zh":"无辅助写作是指在目标语言中写作时不使用任何工具——不用词典、语法检查器，也不用AI帮助。只有你和你的大脑。"}},{"id":"why-do-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why Do It","zh":"为什么要做"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Unassisted writing is a focus on fluidity and getting words out onto the page. It also reveals holes in your knowledge (words you can't remember, unclear grammar constructions, accurate expression of ideas), but leaves a trace in the way speech doesn't. You can't hide behind unclear pronunciation. Each word is on the page, spelled out, which also makes it perfect for review.","zh":"无辅助写作专注于表达的流畅性，以及把词语写到页面上。它也会暴露你知识中的空缺（想不起的词、不清晰的语法结构、准确表达想法的能力），但会像口语无法做到的那样留下痕迹。你无法躲在含混不清的发音后面。每个词都写在页面上、拼写清楚，因此也非常适合复习。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It also builds fluency of expression. Without the option to look things up, your brain is forced to work with what it has — retrieving words, constructing sentences, and expressing ideas from memory. This is the same skill you need for speaking.","zh":"它还会提升表达流利度。由于无法查找内容，你的大脑只能利用已有知识——从记忆中提取词语、构造句子，并表达想法。这正是口语所需要的技能。"}},{"id":"how-to-do-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Do It","zh":"操作方法"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Just write. Journal entries, stream-of-consciousness, descriptions of your day, reactions to something you read. Don't worry about mistakes — the goal is volume and fluency, not accuracy. If you don't know a word, try to express the idea differently. If you're not sure about grammar, go with your gut.","zh":"直接写就好。可以写日记、意识流、对一天的描述，或读完某些内容后的反应。不必担心错误——目标是增加写作量和流利度，而不是追求准确性。如果不知道某个词，尝试换一种方式表达意思。如果不确定语法，就凭直觉写下去。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"A spell checker isn't really a tool, but it's still better to turn it off for this. You get fewer angry red squiggles jumping out at you.","zh":"拼写检查器严格来说不算工具，但进行这项练习时，最好还是把它关掉。这样就不会有那么多令人烦躁的红色波浪线跳出来。"}},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"提示"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Set a timer (10-15 minutes) and write without stopping","zh":"设定计时器（10—15分钟），不停地写"},{"en":"Don't go back and edit as you write — save that for <a href=\"/roadmap/library/writing-analysis\">Writing Analysis</a>","zh":"写作时不要回头修改——把修改留给<a href=\"/roadmap/library/writing-analysis\">写作分析</a>"},{"en":"If you get stuck, write about being stuck (\"I don't know what to say, but I need to keep writing...\")","zh":"如果卡住了，就写下自己卡住的状态（“我不知道该说什么，但我需要继续写下去……”）"},{"en":"Save your unassisted writing for later analysis — it's a goldmine of error patterns","zh":"保存你的无辅助写作，留待日后分析——其中蕴藏着大量错误模式"}]},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Unassisted writing is introduced in Phase 5A alongside assisted writing.","zh":"无辅助写作在阶段5A与有辅助写作一起引入。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
